# Leaderboard service — project context

## Fixed semantics — do not change without an ADR
- **Replace on different score.** A submit overwrites the stored score when the
  value differs (higher or lower). Equal resubmit is a no-op (`>`, not needed;
  equality short-circuits). `improved` is true only when the new score is
  strictly greater.
- **Ordering key:** `(-score, achieved_seq, user_id)`.
- **Ranks** are 1-indexed and unique.
- **Scores** are `StrictInt` in `[score_min, score_max]` (negatives allowed;
  floats rejected).
- **IDs:** `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,id_max_len}$`.
- Top X on unknown/empty game → 200 empty `entries`. Surroundings miss → 404.
- Surroundings default `window=1` (one above, one below).
- First entry → 201 + Location; later → 200.
- **Global score** = sum of current scores on every game; recompute by walking
  `by_user` (no second SortedList). Entries include `games_played`.

## File map
- `app/domain/leaderboard.py`, `app/infra/store.py`, `app/api/leaderboard.py`,
  `app/api/schemas.py`, `app/errors.py`, `app/config.py`
- Docs: `DESIGN.md`, `DECISIONS.md`, `SPEC.md`, `docs/architecture.md`
- Checklist: `tests/test_checklist_cases.py` (cases 1–53)

## Invariants
1. dict and SortedList stay in sync.
2. compute new key → remove old → add new.
3. no `await` in store RMW; single uvicorn worker.
